          MOTIVI DEL FALLIMENTO (seleziona quello applicabile):
          - originalScriptRealityCheck: FAIL (Probabile allucinazione da memoria)
          - promptRealityCheck: FAIL (OPZIONE A VIOLATION: hai inserito in aiPrompts persone, oggetti o azioni non presenti nel video originale)
          - INFERRED / ADDED VIOLATION (aiPrompts): Hai inserito elementi basati su inferenza narrativa o aggiunta di contesto. aiPrompts deve contenere SOLO ciÃƒÂ² che ÃƒÂ¨ VISIBILE o CONSEGUENZA FISICA DIRETTA.
          - STATIC CONTENT LOCK VIOLATION: Se il contenuto ÃƒÂ¨ un POSTER/FLYER, aiPrompts deve contenere SOLO fisicitÃƒÂ  della carta. Vietato inferire luci (es. "side window"), api vere (es. 3D objects), stati mentali (es. "in a hurry").
          - MANDATORY EVENT ALIGNMENT VIOLATION: eventCategory ÃƒÂ¨ 'EVENTO REALE' o 'ESPERIENZA CONCRETA' ma l'intero output (selectedEvent, script, alternativePrompt) ÃƒÂ¨ centrato su dettagli secondari o superfici informative (decorative_detail, informational_surface) invece che sul nucleo dell'azione (core_action, primary_real_world_activity). DEVI cambiare il focus.
          ${structuralFailed ? `- RECENT SYSTEM ERROR: ${structuralFailReason}` : ""}
          - BYPASS/BOOST VIOLATION: Hai inserito elementi CREATIVI (overlay, testo, emoji, 3D, nuove scene) in aiPrompts. Questi DEVONO stare solo in alternativePrompt. aiPrompts deve restare fedele alla fonte (pur se piÃƒÂ¹ intenso).
          - CONTINUITY FAIL-SAFE TRIGGERED: Hai inserito termini promozionali ("Scopri", "Ecco", inviti) o un aesthetic da brochure turistica ("honey macro aesthetic", "rustic table") in ALMENO UNA PARTE dell'output. NON ÃƒË† AMMESSO IN NESSUNA PARTE.
          - MISSING EVENT TRIGGER O REALITY IMPERFECTION FAIL: Hai generato una piatta osservazione o uno script/prompt troppo "costruito", "letterario" o "plastico", ignorando l'obbligo di rendere il momento un "imprevisto casuale e imperfetto".
          - ALTERNATIVE PROMPT TOO WEAK: "alternativePrompt" ÃƒÂ¨ stato generato ma ÃƒÂ¨ solo una variante descrittiva di "aiPrompts", fallendo nell'iniettare vero Event-Trigger, dubbio, o frizione.
          - SELECTION ERROR / HIERARCHY VIOLATION: Hai privilegiato un dettaglio curioso secondario (es. decorative_detail) ignorando o oscurando il vero evento (es. primary_real_world_activity) identificato nel testo.

          CORREZIONE OBBLIGATORIA:
          1. RE-ISPEZIONA l'intero JSON e purga la promozione ovunque.
          2. GERARCHIA EDITORIALE: Se rilevi un evento reale, esso DEVE essere il fulcro di selectedEvent, script e humanVerdict. I dettagli curiosi sono solo hook, non il tema.
          3. CREA UN EVENT TRIGGER E APPLICA LA REALITY IMPERFECTION: Scegli un momento anomalo. Raccontalo NON con lunghe frasi perfette, MA con frammenti, reazioni spontanee o inquadrature distratte/crude.
          3. Lo script DEVE essere frammentario e concitato (azione cruda), niente descrizioni passive, nÃƒÂ© natura contemplativa, nÃƒÂ© prosa noiosa.
          4. Tutto l'output deve rimanere access-driven e EVENT-DRIVEN dall'inizio alla fine.
          5. I prompt DEVONO focalizzarsi sull'evento anomalo senza tentare in maniera affannosa di raccontare ogni passo, dando invece un senso di "rubato per caso".
          6. Se sdopi in alternativePrompt, questo DEVE ESSERE CHIARAMENTE PIÃƒâ„¢ FORTE, TRASFORMATIVO e CURIOSITY-DRIVEN rispetto ad aiPrompts.
          ${viralBoost50k ? `7. Ã°Å¸â€Â¥ VIRAL BOOST 50K ACTIVE: alternativePrompt DEVE avere un hook entro 1.5s, eliminare frasi neutre e usare un linguaggio diretto/crudo. aiPrompts deve aumentare velocitÃƒÂ  e instabilitÃƒÂ  camera restando 100% fedele.` : ""}
          ${viralBoost50k ? "8" : "7"}. Usa obbligatoriamente il blocco "validationTrace" per dichiarare cosa hai corretto.
        `,
        });
      }

      let useFormalSchema = true;
      response = await executeWithNetworkRetry(async (currentAi, dynamicModel) => {
        try {
          return await currentAi.models.generateContent({
            model: dynamicModel || model,
            contents: { parts: currentParts },
            config: {
              systemInstruction: systemInstruction,
              responseMimeType: "application/json",
              ...(useFormalSchema ? { responseSchema: schema } : {}),
            },
          });
        } catch (e: any) {
          const errorMsg = e.message || String(e);
          if (errorMsg.includes("Constraint is too tall") || errorMsg.includes("is too big") || (e.status === 400 && isDeepAnalysis)) {
             logger.warn("[Gemini] Schema too complex for model constraint (too tall), falling back to raw JSON mode...");
             useFormalSchema = false;
             // Retry immediately in the same attempt without schema
             return await currentAi.models.generateContent({
               model: dynamicModel || model,
               contents: { parts: currentParts },
               config: {
                 systemInstruction: systemInstruction + (systemInstruction.includes("JSON") ? "" : "\n\nIMPORTANT: Return a VALID JSON document matching the required structure. Ensure all fields are present."),
                 responseMimeType: "application/json",
               },
             });
          }
          throw e;
        }
      },
        3,
        fallbackOp as any,
        420000, // 7 minutes timeout for large analysis
        apiKey,
        onProgress,
        model,
        trace,
        "Video Analysis Generation",
        currentModelTier as "flash" | "pro"
      );

      const rawParsed = safeParseJSON(response.text || "{}");
      const baseResult = Array.isArray(rawParsed) ? (rawParsed[0] || {}) : rawParsed;
      result = ensureFullAnalysisStructure(baseResult);
      if (hasActiveVideoEvidence && (!result.sourceType || /STATIC_IMAGE|POSTER|FLYER/i.test(String(result.sourceType)))) {
        result.sourceType = "REAL_VIDEO";
      }

      // Resolve Universal Content Matrix
      const matrix = resolveUniversalContentMatrix(result);
      result.contentNature = matrix.contentNature;
      result.primaryEngine = matrix.primaryEngine;
      currentNature = result.contentNature as ContentNature;

        // Normalize aiPrompts if the LLM outputted semantic variants like aiPrompt or aiPromptGenerated
        if (!result.aiPrompts && (result.aiPrompt || result.aiPromptGenerated || result["AI PROMPT"])) {
          result.aiPrompts = result.aiPrompt || result.aiPromptGenerated || result["AI PROMPT"];
        }
        normalizeGeneratedPromptFields(result);
      
      // Inject audio anchor details into result
      if (audioAnchor) {
        result.audioVerified = audioAnchor.audioVerified;
        result.audioSource = audioAnchor.audioSource;
        result.transcriptStatus = audioAnchor.audioVerified ? "VERIFIED_TRANSCRIPT" : "AUDIO_NOT_VERIFIED";
        result.verifiedTranscript = audioAnchor.literalTranscript;
        result.scriptConfidence = audioAnchor.scriptConfidence;
        result.dialogueAnalysis = audioAnchor.verifiedInlineVideoSummary;
        result.scriptFaithfulness = audioAnchor.dialogueFaithfulnessScore;
        result.scriptSourceMode = audioAnchor.scriptSourceMode;
        result.analysisRoutingMode = audioAnchor.audioVerified ? "FRAME_PLUS_AUDIO_ANCHOR" : "FRAME_ONLY";
        result.promptSafetyMode = audioAnchor.audioVerified ? "AUDIO_VERIFIED" : "VISUAL_SAFE";
      }
      
      if (primaryPurposeLock) {
         result.primaryPurposeLock = primaryPurposeLock;
      }
      if (functionalRoleLock) {
         result.functionalRoleLock = functionalRoleLock;
      }
      if (ideaAnchorLock) {
         result.ideaAnchorLock = ideaAnchorLock;
      }
      if (transformationOutput) {
         result.transformationOutput = transformationOutput;
      }

      const groqCreativeInput: GroqCreativeStudioInput = {
        sourceKind: result.sourceType === "POSTER"
          ? "POSTER"
          : ((result.sourceType === "STATIC_IMAGE" || result.sourceType === "FLYER")
            ? "IMAGE"
            : (file || providedFileUri ? "VIDEO" : (result.originalScript ? "SCRIPT" : "TEXT_IDEA"))),
        platform: pomelli?.platform,
        genre: pomelli?.genre,
        sceneMasterPrompt: result.sceneMasterPrompt,
        verifiedTranscript: result.verifiedTranscript,
        originalScript: result.originalScript,
        optimizedScript: result.script,
        visualSummary: result.dialogueAnalysis,
        visibleSurfaceElements: result.visibleSurfaceElements,
        semanticMentions: result.semanticMentions,
        promptInventory: result.promptInventory,
        selectedEvent: result.eventQualitySelector?.selectedEvent || result.eventQualitySelector?.evaluation,
        viralStructure: result.viralStructure,
        externalMarketData,
        userGoal: textInput,
        targetModels: ["Sora", "Kling", "Seedance", "Sendance", "Veo", "Cover", "Publishing Kit"],
        detectedSourceLanguage: result.detectedSourceLanguage,
      };
      const groqCreativeEligible = shouldRunGroqCreativeStudio(groqCreativeInput);
      if (groqCreativeEligible) {
        const creativeStudio = await runGroqCreativeStudio(groqCreativeInput, result);
        result = { ...result, ...creativeStudio.result };
      } else {
        logger.info('[GROQ_CREATIVE_STUDIO_SKIPPED]', {
          reason: !hasGroqApiKey()
            ? 'GROQ_NOT_CONFIGURED'
            : !(groqCreativeInput.sceneMasterPrompt || groqCreativeInput.verifiedTranscript || groqCreativeInput.originalScript || groqCreativeInput.visualSummary || (Array.isArray(groqCreativeInput.visibleSurfaceElements) && groqCreativeInput.visibleSurfaceElements.length > 0) || (Array.isArray(groqCreativeInput.semanticMentions) && groqCreativeInput.semanticMentions.length > 0))
              ? 'INSUFFICIENT_CREATIVE_CONTEXT'
              : 'ELIGIBILITY_FALSE',
          hasGroqConfigured: hasGroqApiKey(),
          hasSceneMaster: !!groqCreativeInput.sceneMasterPrompt,
          hasTranscript: !!groqCreativeInput.verifiedTranscript,
          hasOriginalScript: !!groqCreativeInput.originalScript,
          hasVisualSummary: !!groqCreativeInput.visualSummary,
          hasVisibleSurfaceElements: Array.isArray(groqCreativeInput.visibleSurfaceElements) && groqCreativeInput.visibleSurfaceElements.length > 0,
          hasSemanticMentions: Array.isArray(groqCreativeInput.semanticMentions) && groqCreativeInput.semanticMentions.length > 0,
        });
      }
      
      // --- LAYER 1: EVENT DETECTION ---
      let payloadSourceType = result.sourceType || "";
      let enforcedVisibleElements = Array.isArray(result.visibleSurfaceElements)
        ? [...result.visibleSurfaceElements]
        : [];
      let staticViolation = false;
      const eventCategory = result.eventQualitySelector?.eventCategory;
      const isFileStatic = !providedFileUri && file && file.type.startsWith('image/');
      const isStrictStatic = isStrictStaticSourceType(payloadSourceType) || isFileStatic;

      structuralFailed = false;
      structuralFailReason = "";
      bypassViolation = false;

       // --- LAYER 2: EVENT MATERIALIZATION (BEFORE STATIC FILTER) ---
      try {
        if (isStrictStatic) {
          logger.info("[PIPELINE_BRANCH] STATIC_IMAGE detected. EVENT_MATERIALIZATION/VALIDATION HARD-DISABLED.");
          // Ensure no event category is used for static image downstream logic
          result.eventQualitySelector = { ...result.eventQualitySelector, eventCategory: "NONE" };
          result.script = coerceLooseText(result.script) || coerceLooseText(result.originalScript) || "";
        } else {
            result.script = coerceLooseText(result.script);
            result.originalScript = coerceLooseText(result.originalScript);

            if (!result.script) {
              result.script = result.originalScript || "";
            }

            logger.info("[SCRIPT_PIPELINE_CHECK]", {
              scriptLength: result.script?.length || 0,
              originalScriptLength: result.originalScript?.length || 0,
              usingFallbackFromOriginal: !result.script
            });

            if (!result.script) {
              throw new Error("EMPTY_SCRIPT_PIPELINE: Sia script che originalScript sono vuoti. Impossibile procedere con la materializzazione.");
            }

            if (isValidatorCompatible('eventMaterialization', currentNature)) {
              enforceEventMaterialization(result, eventCategory || "", contentHierarchy?.primarySubject, contentHierarchy);
            }
        }

        // --- LAYER 2.1: EVENT CORE DOMINANCE HARDENING ---
        const hasActionCore = !!(contentHierarchy?.actionCore && contentHierarchy.actionCore.length > 5);
        const isActionIntent = contentHierarchy?.dominantPurpose?.toUpperCase().includes('ACTION') || 
                               contentHierarchy?.contentNature?.toUpperCase().includes('ACTION');
                               
        if (isValidatorCompatible('eventCore', currentNature) && !isStrictStatic && (eventCategory === "EVENTO REALE" || eventCategory === "ESPERIENZA CONCRETA") && !hasActionCore && !isActionIntent) {
          const experienceRegex = /\b(partecipano|agiscono|performano|eseguono|osservano|interagiscono|ascoltano|si radunano|visita|partecipazione|esperienza|incontro|esibizione|performance|azione|attivitÃƒÂ |scoprono|scopre)\b/gi;
          const accessRegex = /\b(percorso|indicazioni|posizione|dettaglio_marginale|informational_surface|decorative_detail)\b/gi;

          const scriptText = result.script || "";
          const selectedEventText = result.selectedEvent || result.eventQualitySelector?.selectedEvent || "";
          const alternativeText = result.alternativePrompt || "";

          // 1. Dominance calculation (Script + SelectedEvent + AlternativePrompt)
          const coreText = `${scriptText} ${selectedEventText} ${alternativeText}`;
          const experienceCount = (coreText.match(experienceRegex) || []).length;
          const accessCount = (coreText.match(accessRegex) || []).length;
          const isExperienceDominant = experienceCount > accessCount;

          logger.info("[EVENT_CORE_VALIDATION]", {
            eventCategory,
            experienceCount,
            accessCount,
            selectedEvent: selectedEventText,
            isExperienceDominant
          });

          // 2. Dominance check
          if (!isExperienceDominant) {
            logger.error("[EVENT_PRIORITY_VIOLATION]", { experienceCount, accessCount });
            throw new Error("EVENT_PRIORITY_VIOLATION Ã¢â‚¬â€œ access details dominate or experience missing");
          }

          // 3. BLOCCO selectedEvent ACCESS-DRIVEN for ESPERIENZA CONCRETA
          const selectedEventAccessCount = (selectedEventText.match(accessRegex) || []).length;
          const selectedEventExperienceCount = (selectedEventText.match(experienceRegex) || []).length;

          // Per ESPERIENZA CONCRETA, il divieto ÃƒÂ¨ assoluto: selectedEvent non puÃƒÂ² essere accesso/percorso
          if (eventCategory === "ESPERIENZA CONCRETA" || (selectedEventAccessCount > 0 && selectedEventExperienceCount === 0)) {
             // Re-check specific access terms even if experience present, for concrete experience we want ACTION first
             const hasHardAccessKeywords = /percorso|indicazioni|decorative_detail/i.test(selectedEventText);
             if (hasHardAccessKeywords && selectedEventExperienceCount === 0) {
               logger.error("[EVENT_ACCESS_DOMINANT_SELECTED_EVENT]", { selectedEvent: selectedEventText, eventCategory });
               throw new Error("EVENT_ACCESS_DOMINANT_SELECTED_EVENT Ã¢â‚¬â€œ selectedEvent cannot be a path/access element in ESPERIENZA CONCRETA");
             }
          }

          // 4. BLOCCO alternativePrompt ARRIVO SENZA SEGUITO
          const altAccessCount = (alternativeText.match(accessRegex) || []).length;
          const altExperienceCount = (alternativeText.match(experienceRegex) || []).length;

          if (altAccessCount > 0 && altExperienceCount === 0) {
            logger.error("[ALT_PROMPT_NO_EXPERIENCE_FOLLOWUP]", { alternativePrompt: alternativeText });
            throw new Error("ALT_PROMPT_NO_EXPERIENCE_FOLLOWUP");
          }
        }
      } catch (e: any) {
        logger.error("[EVENT_MATERIALIZATION_ERROR]", { error: e.message });
        if (
          e.message.includes("EMPTY_SCRIPT_PIPELINE") || 
          e.message.includes("EVENT_PRIORITY_VIOLATION") ||
          e.message.includes("EVENT_CORE_MISSING_EXPERIENCE") ||
          e.message.includes("EVENT_ACCESS_DOMINANT_SELECTED_EVENT") ||
          e.message.includes("ALT_PROMPT_NO_EXPERIENCE_FOLLOWUP")
        ) {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = e.message;
        }
      }

      // --- LAYER 3: STATIC SAFETY (LAST STEP) ---
      if (isStrictStatic && isValidatorCompatible('staticAsset', currentNature)) {
        logger.info("[Gemini][StaticGate] Applying FINAL static safety stripping.");
        const strip = (p: string) => stripStaticSourceViolations(p, enforcedVisibleElements, eventCategory);
        
          if (typeof result.aiPrompts === "string") result.aiPrompts = strip(result.aiPrompts);
          if (typeof result.promptSora15s === "string") result.promptSora15s = strip(result.promptSora15s);
          if (typeof result.promptSora12s === "string") result.promptSora12s = strip(result.promptSora12s);
          if (typeof result.promptKling === "string") result.promptKling = strip(result.promptKling);
          if (typeof result.promptVeo === "string") result.promptVeo = strip(result.promptVeo);
          if (typeof result.klingPrompt10s === "string") result.klingPrompt10s = strip(result.klingPrompt10s);
          if (typeof result.klingPrompt15s === "string") result.klingPrompt15s = strip(result.klingPrompt15s);
          if (typeof result.seedancePrompt15s === "string") result.seedancePrompt15s = strip(result.seedancePrompt15s);
          if (typeof result.sendancePrompt15s === "string") result.sendancePrompt15s = strip(result.sendancePrompt15s);
          if (typeof result.veo3Prompt8s === "string") result.veo3Prompt8s = strip(result.veo3Prompt8s);
          if (typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s === "string") result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s = strip(result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s);
          if (typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s === "string") result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s = strip(result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s);
          if (typeof result.alternativePrompt === "string") result.alternativePrompt = strip(result.alternativePrompt);
          if (typeof result.script === "string") result.script = strip(result.script);
        }

      logger.warn("[Gemini][StaticGate][PROBE-ENTER]", {
        payloadSourceType,
        hasAiPrompts:
          typeof result.aiPrompts === "string" &&
          result.aiPrompts.trim().length > 0,
        staticSourceTextPreview: collectStaticSourcePromptText(result).slice(
          0,
          200,
        ),
        staticViolations: [],
      });

      if (isStrictStaticSourceType(payloadSourceType) && isValidatorCompatible('staticAsset', currentNature)) {
        logger.warn("[Gemini][StaticGate][PROBE-IN-BRANCH]", {
          payloadSourceType,
          hasAiPrompts:
            typeof result.aiPrompts === "string" &&
            result.aiPrompts.trim().length > 0,
          staticSourceTextPreview: collectStaticSourcePromptText(result).slice(
            0,
            200,
          ),
          staticViolations: [],
        });

        enforcedVisibleElements = [
          "paper",
          "text",
          "map",
          "print",
          "ink",
          "physical surface",
          "poster",
          "sign",
          "informational_surface",
        ];
        result.visibleSurfaceElements = enforcedVisibleElements; // Overwrite parsed object

        const staticSourceText = collectStaticSourcePromptText(result);
        const staticViolations = findStaticSourceViolations(result);

        const STATIC_CAMERA_MOTION_TERMS =
          /\b(?:scan|macro\s+scan|gliding|zoom|focus\s+shifts?|camera\s+maintains|camera\s+focuses|drifts?|drifting)\b/i;
        if (hasRealStaticViolation(STATIC_CAMERA_MOTION_TERMS, staticSourceText, "borderline-camera-motion")) {
          staticViolations.push("borderline-camera-motion");
        }

        logger.warn("[Gemini][StaticGate][PROBE-VIOLATIONS]", {
          payloadSourceType,
          hasAiPrompts:
            typeof result.aiPrompts === "string" &&
            result.aiPrompts.trim().length > 0,
          staticSourceTextPreview: staticSourceText.slice(0, 200),
          staticViolations,
        });
        const matchedStaticRules = STATIC_SOURCE_VIOLATION_RULES.filter(
          (rule) => staticViolations.includes(rule.label),
        ).map((rule) => ({ label: rule.label, pattern: rule.pattern.source }));

        logger.info("[Gemini][StaticGate] Evaluating static source payload", {
          attempt: attempts,
          sourceType: payloadSourceType,
          staticSourceText,
          staticViolations,
          matchedStaticRules,
        });

        if (staticViolations.length > 0) {
          staticViolation = true;
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = `STATIC CONTENT LOCK VIOLATION: Source-static prompt contains filmed-scene descriptors (${staticViolations.join(", ")}).`;
          if (result.validationTrace)
            result.validationTrace.structuralFailTriggered = true;
          if (!result.viralAudit)
            result.viralAudit = {
              signature: "SYSTEM_FORCED",
              enforcementMarker: "FAIL",
              strategyReasoning: "Static source violation detected",
              enforcementPass: false,
            };
          result.viralAudit.enforcementPass = false;
          logger.warn(
            "[Gemini] Static Content Lock violation detected in static prompt set on try " +
              attempts,
            { staticViolations },
          );

          const traceTargets = [
            "hand-thumb-finger",
            "shaky-shake-jitter-micro-movement",
            "camera-jitters",
            "borderline-camera-motion",
            "breath-whisper-dialogue-voice",
            "fold-crease-crinkle-flutter"
          ];

          for (const target of traceTargets) {
            if (staticViolations.includes(target)) {
              let checkPattern;
              if (target === "borderline-camera-motion") {
                checkPattern = new RegExp(STATIC_CAMERA_MOTION_TERMS.source, "gi");
              } else {
                const rule = STATIC_SOURCE_VIOLATION_RULES.find((r) => r.label === target);
                if (rule) {
                  checkPattern = new RegExp(rule.pattern.source, "gi");
                }
              }

              if (checkPattern) {
                const fieldsToCheck: Record<string, string> = {
                  aiPrompts:
                    typeof result.aiPrompts === "string" ? result.aiPrompts : "",
                  promptSora15s:
                    typeof result.promptSora15s === "string"
                      ? result.promptSora15s
                      : "",
                  promptSora12s:
                    typeof result.promptSora12s === "string"
                      ? result.promptSora12s
                      : "",
                  promptKling:
                    typeof result.promptKling === "string"
                      ? result.promptKling
                      : "",
                  promptVeo:
                    typeof result.promptVeo === "string" ? result.promptVeo : "",
                  soraPrompt15s:
                    typeof result.soraPrompt15s === "string"
                      ? result.soraPrompt15s
                      : "",
                  soraPrompt12s:
                    typeof result.soraPrompt12s === "string"
                      ? result.soraPrompt12s
                      : "",
                  klingPrompt10s:
                    typeof result.klingPrompt10s === "string"
                      ? result.klingPrompt10s
                      : "",
                  klingPrompt15s:
                    typeof result.klingPrompt15s === "string"
                      ? result.klingPrompt15s
                      : "",
                  seedancePrompt15s:
                    typeof result.seedancePrompt15s === "string"
                      ? result.seedancePrompt15s
                      : "",
                  sendancePrompt15s:
                    typeof result.sendancePrompt15s === "string"
                      ? result.sendancePrompt15s
                      : "",
                  klingPrompt:
                    typeof result.klingPrompt === "string"
                      ? result.klingPrompt
                      : "",
                  veo3Prompt8s:
                    typeof result.veo3Prompt8s === "string"
                      ? result.veo3Prompt8s
                      : "",
                  veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s:
                    typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s === "string"
                      ? result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s
                      : "",
                  veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s:
                    typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s === "string"
                      ? result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s
                      : "",
                  veoPrompt:
                    typeof result.veoPrompt === "string" ? result.veoPrompt : "",
                  alternativePrompt:
                    typeof result.alternativePrompt === "string"
                      ? result.alternativePrompt
                      : "",
                  publishingKit:
                    typeof result.publishingKit === "string"
                      ? result.publishingKit
                      : result.publishingKit
                        ? JSON.stringify(result.publishingKit)
                        : "",
                  "viralAudit.enforcementMarker":
                    typeof result.viralAudit?.enforcementMarker === "string"
                      ? result.viralAudit.enforcementMarker
                      : "",
                  "parsedKit.altScene":
                    typeof result.parsedKit?.altScene === "string"
                      ? result.parsedKit.altScene
                      : "",
                  "parsedKit.altTwist":
                    typeof result.parsedKit?.altTwist === "string"
                      ? result.parsedKit.altTwist
                      : "",
                  "parsedKit.musicalAnalysisIt":
                    typeof result.parsedKit?.musicalAnalysisIt === "string"
                      ? result.parsedKit.musicalAnalysisIt
                      : "",
                  "parsedKit.musicalAnalysisEn":
                    typeof result.parsedKit?.musicalAnalysisEn === "string"
                      ? result.parsedKit.musicalAnalysisEn
                      : "",
                  readyAlternative: Array.isArray(result.readyAlternative)
                    ? result.readyAlternative.join(" ")
                    : typeof result.readyAlternative === "string"
                      ? result.readyAlternative
                      : "",
                  "parsedKit.readyAlternative": Array.isArray(
                    result.parsedKit?.readyAlternative,
                  )
                    ? result.parsedKit.readyAlternative.join(" ")
                    : typeof result.parsedKit?.readyAlternative === "string"
                      ? result.parsedKit.readyAlternative
                      : "",
                };

                for (const [fieldName, text] of Object.entries(fieldsToCheck)) {
                  if (!text) continue;
                  checkPattern.lastIndex = 0;
                  let match;
                  while ((match = checkPattern.exec(text)) !== null) {
                    if (match.index === checkPattern.lastIndex) {
                      checkPattern.lastIndex++;
                    }
                    const matchTerm = match[0];
                    const start = Math.max(0, match.index - 50);
                    const end = Math.min(
                      text.length,
                      match.index + matchTerm.length + 50,
                    );
                    const snippet = text
                      .substring(start, end)
                      .replace(/\n/g, " ");
                    logger.warn(
                      `[Gemini][StaticGate][TRACE] Found [${target}] in ${fieldName} | Term: '${matchTerm}' | Snippet: '...${snippet}...'`,
                    );
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }

        // Sanitize inventory and physics to prevent downstream fidelity gate failures using a Strict Allowlist
        const eventTerms = normalizeTextForEnforcement(result.selectedEvent || "");
        const staticAllowlist =
          /\b(paper|printed|print|ink|text|map|poster|informational_surface|sign|surface|texture|grain|fiber|fibres|fibers|edge|edges|fold|folds|crease|creases|wrinkle|wrinkles|aged|weathered|ink|marker|handwritten|calligraphy|layout|design|border|frame|graphic)\b/i;
        
        if (Array.isArray(result.promptInventory)) {
          result.promptInventory = result.promptInventory.filter(
            (item) => {
              if (typeof item !== "string") return false;
              if (staticAllowlist.test(item)) return true;
              return eventTerms.some(term => item.toLowerCase().includes(term));
            }
          );
        }
        if (Array.isArray(result.physicsWhitelist)) {
          result.physicsWhitelist = result.physicsWhitelist.filter(
            (item) => {
              if (typeof item !== "string") return false;
              if (staticAllowlist.test(item)) return true;
              return eventTerms.some(term => item.toLowerCase().includes(term));
            }
          );
        }
      }

      if (result.executionDebugBlock) {
        const debug = result.executionDebugBlock;
        const failedChecks = [];
        if (debug.dialogueMappingCheck === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("dialogueMappingCheck");
        if (debug.externalDataLanguageMatch === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("externalDataLanguageMatch");
        if (debug.externalDataCultureMatch === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("externalDataCultureMatch");
        if (debug.coverPromptGenerated === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("coverPromptGenerated");
        if (debug.outputCompletenessCheck === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("outputCompletenessCheck");
        if (debug.scoreConsistencyCheck === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("scoreConsistencyCheck");
        if (debug.transformationOverreach === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("transformationOverreach");
        if (debug.noActivation === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("noActivation");
        if (debug.sceneEvolutionCheck === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("sceneEvolutionCheck");
        if (debug.languageSeparationCheck === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("languageSeparationCheck");
        if (debug.directivePriorityCheck === "FAIL")
          failedChecks.push("directivePriorityCheck");

        if (debug.transformationOverreach === "FAIL") {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = "TRANSFORMATION_OVERREACH: Il sistema ha inventato eventi o dinamiche non deducibili dal contenuto (Hard Fail).";
          truthStatus.failedModules.push("TRANSFORMATION_OVERREACH_GUARD");
        }
        if (debug.noActivation === "FAIL") {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = "NO_ACTIVATION: Mancato gancio virale. Il sistema ÃƒÂ¨ rimasto troppo conservativo senza attivare il potenziale del frame (Hard Fail).";
          truthStatus.failedModules.push("NO_ACTIVATION_GUARD");
        }
        
        // --- LAYER 2.1: SCENE_EVOLUTION_CHECK ---
        if (debug.sceneEvolutionCheck === "FAIL" || (result.sceneEvolution && result.sceneEvolution.isMeaningful === false)) {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = "SCENE_EVOLUTION_FAIL: Output piatto senza trasformazione significativa. ÃƒË† richiesta un'evoluzione visibile tra inizio e fine (Requirement Fiscale).";
          truthStatus.failedModules.push("SCENE_EVOLUTION_GUARD");
        }

        // --- LAYER 2.2: MICRO_TENSION_CHECK ---
        if (!result.microTension) {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = "MICRO_TENSION_FAIL: Manca l'attivazione minima creativa (microTension) obbligatoria.";
          truthStatus.failedModules.push("MICRO_TENSION_GUARD");
        } else {
          const mt = result.microTension;
          if (sourceTypeLocked === 'STATIC_IMAGE') {
            if (mt.mode !== 'generate' || !mt.type || mt.type === 'none') {
              structuralFailed = true;
              structuralFailReason = "MICRO_TENSION_FAIL: Un input STATIC deve necessariamente generare tensione inventata per non essere piatto (mode=generate richiesto).";
              truthStatus.failedModules.push("MICRO_TENSION_GUARD");
            }
          } else if (sourceTypeLocked && (sourceTypeLocked.includes('VIDEO') || sourceTypeLocked.includes('ANIMATED'))) {
            const forbiddenInvented = ["gaze anomaly", "interrupted action", "off-frame trigger", "contrast behavior"];
            if (mt.mode !== 'extract' || forbiddenInvented.includes(mt.type)) {
              structuralFailed = true;
              structuralFailReason = `MICRO_TENSION_FAIL: Un input VIDEO non deve includere eventi inventati o surreali non presenti nel video originale. Tipo rintracciato: ${mt.type}. Mode dev'essere 'extract'.`;
              truthStatus.failedModules.push("MICRO_TENSION_GUARD");
            }
          }
        }

        // --- LAYER 2.3: CREATIVE_DEPTH vs POTENTIAL CHECK ---
        const depthLevels: Record<string, number> = { "low": 1, "medium": 2, "high": 3 };
        const depthVal = depthLevels[String(result.creativeDepth || "").toLowerCase()] || 0;
        const potentialVal = depthLevels[String(result.creativePotential || "").toLowerCase()] || 0;
        
        if (depthVal > potentialVal) {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = `CREATIVE_DEPTH_OVERREACH: L'output cerca di esprimere una profonditÃƒÂ  creativa (${result.creativeDepth}) superiore al potenziale intrinseco dell'input (${result.creativePotential}). Questo causa over-promising o allucinazioni.`;
          truthStatus.failedModules.push("CREATIVE_DEPTH_GUARD");
        }

        // Critical Fidelity & Structural Checks
        let fidelityFailed =
          debug.originalScriptRealityCheck === "FAIL" ||
          debug.promptRealityCheck === "FAIL";

        // --- DUAL-INVENTORY ENFORCEMENT (EXTERNAL GATE) ---
        const isEventExplicitlyRequestedSub = eventCategory === "EVENTO REALE" || eventCategory === "ESPERIENZA CONCRETA";
        const physicsWhitelistForFidelity = (isStrictStaticSourceType(payloadSourceType) && !isEventExplicitlyRequestedSub)
          ? []
          : result.physicsWhitelist;

        if (isValidatorCompatible('fidelityGate', currentNature)) {
          const { violations: fidelityViolations, type: violationType } =
            verifyFidelity(
              enforcedVisibleElements,
              result.semanticMentions,
              physicsWhitelistForFidelity,
              result.promptInventory,
              eventCategory,
              payloadSourceType
            );

          if (violationType !== "None" && fidelityViolations.length > 0) {
            structuralFailed = true;
            if (!staticViolation) {
              structuralFailReason = `FIDELITY GATE: ${violationType} Violation detected. Element '${fidelityViolations[0]}' is non-visible or belongs to semanticMentions. Rimuoverlo o spostarlo in alternativePrompt.`;
            }
            logger.warn(
              `[Gemini] ${violationType} Violation detected in promptInventory: ${fidelityViolations[0]} on try ${attempts}`,
            );
          }
        }

        if (isValidatorCompatible('integrityCheck', currentNature)) {
          const integrityViolations = integrityCrossCheck(
            result.aiPrompts || "",
            result.promptInventory || [],
          );
          if (integrityViolations.length > 0) {
            // Relaxed: Just warn about Integrity Violations instead of completely blocking
            logger.warn(
              `[Gemini] Integrity Violation Warning detected in aiPrompts: ${integrityViolations[0]} on try ${attempts}`,
            );
          }
        }

        if (result.viralAudit?.enforcementPass === false && !structuralFailed) {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason = "enforcementPass is false explicitly";
        }

        // --- LAYER 2.2: CONTENT_HIERARCHY_COHERENCE_CHECK (mandatory if plan exists) ---
        if (contentHierarchy) {
          const forbidden = contentHierarchy.forbiddenDominantElements || [];
          const tertiary = contentHierarchy.tertiaryElements || [];
          const primary = [contentHierarchy.primarySubject, contentHierarchy.requiredSceneDestination].filter(Boolean) || [];
          
          const scriptTextLower = String(result.script || "").toLowerCase();
          const selectedEventLower = String(result.selectedEvent || "").toLowerCase();
          const alternativeTextLower = String(result.alternativePrompt || "").toLowerCase();
          const kitTextLower = typeof result.publishingKit === "string" ? result.publishingKit.toLowerCase() : JSON.stringify(result.publishingKit || "").toLowerCase();

          const allOutputs = `${scriptTextLower} ${selectedEventLower} ${alternativeTextLower} ${kitTextLower}`;

          // Critical Violation A: Forbidden element in selectedEvent (the core)
          const forbiddenInCore = forbidden.find(term => {
            const regex = new RegExp(`\\b${term}\\b`, 'gi');
            return regex.test(selectedEventLower);
          });

          // Critical Violation B: Dominance inversion (Forbidden/Tertiary appearing more than Primary)
          let primaryCount = 0;
          primary.forEach(term => {
            const regex = new RegExp(`\\b${term}\\b`, 'gi');
            primaryCount += (allOutputs.match(regex) || []).length;
          });

          let violationCount = 0;
          let violatingTerm = "";
          [...forbidden, ...tertiary].forEach(term => {
            const regex = new RegExp(`\\b${term}\\b`, 'gi');
            const count = (allOutputs.match(regex) || []).length;
            if (count > violationCount) {
              violationCount = count;
              violatingTerm = term;
            }
          });

          const isFailingByCore = !!forbiddenInCore;
          const isFailingByDominance = violationCount > (primaryCount + 1); // allow 1 small delta, but not dominance

          // --- LAYER 2.3: PRIMARY_PURPOSE_LOCK_VALIDATION ---
          let purposeViolation = false;
          if (primaryPurposeLock) {
            const decorationElements = primaryPurposeLock.elementsClassification
              ?.filter((e: any) => e.role === 'DECORATION')
              .map((e: any) => e.element.toLowerCase()) || [];
            
            const hookText = (Array.isArray(result.pubTitoliHookIt) ? result.pubTitoliHookIt.join(" ") : String(result.pubTitoliHookIt || "")).toLowerCase();
            const introText = String(result.script || "").substring(0, 100).toLowerCase(); 
            
            const decorationAsHook = decorationElements.find((dec: string) => hookText.includes(dec));
            const decorationAsOpening = decorationElements.find((dec: string) => introText.includes(dec));

            if (decorationAsHook || decorationAsOpening) {
              purposeViolation = true;
            }
          }

          // --- LAYER 2.4: FUNCTIONAL_ROLE_LOCK_VALIDATION ---
          let functionalViolation = false;
          // Note: functionalRoleLock is a static pre-computed lock. We pass it to the AI as a constraint,
          // but we shouldn't infinitely fail the loop just because the concept was initially marked FAIL.
          
          // --- LAYER 2.5: IDEA_ANCHOR_LOCK_VALIDATION ---
          let anchorViolation = false;
          if (ideaAnchorLock && ideaAnchorLock.lockStatus === 'FAIL') {
             anchorViolation = true; // HARD FAIL RESTORED
          }

          // --- LAYER 2.6: CORE_INTENT_DRIFT_CHECK ---
          let intentDrift = false;
          if (coreIntentClassification) {
            const intent = coreIntentClassification.coreIntent;
            // Script + Event + Titles (IT/EN mixed)
            const outputText = `${result.script} ${result.selectedEvent} ${Array.isArray(result.pubTitoliHookIt) ? result.pubTitoliHookIt.join(" ") : String(result.pubTitoliHookIt || "")} ${String(result.aiPrompts || "")}`.toLowerCase();
            
            if (intent === 'PERSONA') {
              const personaRegex = /\b(chi|lei|lui|persona|uomo|donna|ragazzo|ragazza|attore|protagonista|io|tu|soggetto|volto|sguardo|occhi|sorriso|espressione|person|man|woman|actor|actress|guy|girl|subject|face|eyes|smile|presence|human|gaze|look)\b/i;
              const hasPersonaKeyword = personaRegex.test(outputText);
              
              // Cross-language name/subject verification
              const subjectWords = String(contentHierarchy?.primarySubject || "").toLowerCase().split(/\s+/).filter((w: string) => w.length > 3);
              const hasSubjectWord = subjectWords.some((w: string) => outputText.includes(w));
              
              if (!hasPersonaKeyword && !hasSubjectWord && isValidatorCompatible('dialogueIntent', currentNature)) {
                intentDrift = true;
              }
            } else if (intent === 'PRODOTTO') {
              if (isValidatorCompatible('productDemo', currentNature)) {
                const productRegex = /\b(prodotto|oggetto|articolo|cosa|dispositivo|bene|acquisto|compralo|servizio|dettaglio|materiale|pelle|tessuto|riflesso|product|item|object|device|purchase|buy|service|good|commodity|texture|material|leather|fabric|reflection)\b/i;
                const hasProductKeyword = productRegex.test(outputText);
                
                const subjectWords = String(contentHierarchy?.primarySubject || "").toLowerCase().split(/\s+/).filter((w: string) => w.length > 3);
                const hasSubjectWord = subjectWords.some((w: string) => outputText.includes(w));

                if (!hasProductKeyword && !hasSubjectWord) {
                  intentDrift = true;
                }
              }
            }
          }

          // --- LAYER 2.7: TRANSFORMATION_OVERREACH_CHECK ---
          let transformationOverreach = false;
          if (result.transformationOutput && result.transformationOutput.activationType === 'MICRO_REALISTIC') {
            const microScene = String(result.transformationOutput.microScene || "").toLowerCase();
            const allPrompts = `${result.promptSora15s} ${result.promptSora12s} ${result.promptKling} ${result.promptVeo} ${result.klingPrompt10s || ""} ${result.klingPrompt15s || ""} ${result.seedancePrompt15s || ""} ${result.veo3Prompt8s || ""} ${result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s || ""} ${result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s || ""}`.toLowerCase();
            
            // Se la microScene ÃƒÂ¨ semplice (es. smile) ma i prompt contengono parole complesse o eventi non richiesti
            // Questo ÃƒÂ¨ un controllo euristico semplice: se ci sono troppe parole nuove rispetto alla microScene e al soggetto originale
            const forbiddenInStatic = ["cinematic", "epic", "battle", "running", "explosion", "magic", "flying", "dialogue", "speaking", "talking"];
            const overreachTerm = forbiddenInStatic.find(term => allPrompts.includes(term));
            
            if (overreachTerm) {
              transformationOverreach = true;
            }
          }

          if (isFailingByCore || isFailingByDominance || purposeViolation || functionalViolation || anchorViolation || intentDrift || transformationOverreach) {
            structuralFailed = true;
            structuralFailReason = transformationOverreach ? "TRANSFORMATION_OVERREACH" :
                                   purposeViolation ? "PURPOSE_VIOLATION_DECORATION_AS_HOOK" : 
                                   anchorViolation ? "ANCHOR_DEPENDENCY_VIOLATION" :
                                   functionalViolation ? "FUNCTIONAL_DOMINANCE_VIOLATION" :
                                   intentDrift ? "CORE_INTENT_DRIFT" :
                                   "CONTENT_HIERARCHY_BROKEN";
            logger.error(structuralFailReason, {
              isFailingByCore,
              isFailingByDominance,
              purposeViolation,
              functionalViolation,
              anchorViolation,
              primaryCount,
              violationCount,
              violatingTerm
            });
            lastFailReason = structuralFailReason;
          } else {
             // RUN THE ACTUAL DOMINANCE VALIDATOR (AI-BASED) IN THE RETRY LOOP
             try {
               const { runContentDominanceValidator } = await import("./analysis");
               const generatedAssets = {
                 script: Array.isArray(result.script) ? result.script.join(" ") : (result.script || ""),
                 aiPrompts: result.aiPrompts,
                 hook: Array.isArray(result.pubTitoliHookIt) ? result.pubTitoliHookIt.join(" ") : (result.pubVideoHookIt || result.hook || (result.publishingKit ? (typeof result.publishingKit === 'string' ? result.publishingKit : JSON.stringify(result.publishingKit)) : ""))
               };
               const dominanceCheck = await runContentDominanceValidator(apiKey, contentHierarchy, generatedAssets);
               result.dominanceCheck = dominanceCheck;
               
               if (dominanceCheck.pass === false && dominanceCheck.severity === 'HIGH') {
                   logger.warn("[Gemini Generation] AI Dominance Override Detected inside loop!", dominanceCheck);
                   
                   if (dominanceCheck.dominantElement && contentHierarchy && String(dominanceCheck.dominantElement).toLowerCase() !== String(contentHierarchy.primarySubject || "").toLowerCase()) {
                       // HARD MISMATCH
                       logger.warn("[Gemini Generation] HARD MISMATCH detected. Forcing hierarchy realignment.");
                       dominanceCheck.reason = `HARD MISMATCH: Riallineamento forzato da '${contentHierarchy.primarySubject}' a '${dominanceCheck.dominantElement}'`;
                       contentHierarchy.primarySubject = dominanceCheck.dominantElement;
                       if (result.contentHierarchy) result.contentHierarchy = contentHierarchy;
                       dominanceCheck.pass = true;
                       dominanceCheck.severity = "LOW";
                   } else {
                       structuralFailed = true;
                       structuralFailReason = "DOMINANCE_PLAN_BROKEN_BY_AI: " + dominanceCheck.reason;
                       if (attempts >= maxAttempts && result.viralScore) {
                           result.viralScore = "2.0"; // Drastica penalitÃƒÂ  se non riusciamo a recuperare
                       }
                   }
               }
             } catch (valErr) {
               logger.warn("Dominance validation internal AI module failed inside executeGeneration", valErr);
             }
          }
        }

        // --- LAYER 2.1: EVENT FLOW ENGINE (LEGACY/FALLBACK) ---
        if (!structuralFailed && isValidatorCompatible('actionHierarchy', currentNature)) {
           const eventCoreRegex = /\b(?:evento|esperienza|performance|azione|attivitÃƒÂ |svolgimento|incontro|visita|celebrazione|esibizione|appuntamento|partecipazione|interazione|manifestazione|comedy|sketch|battuta|payoff|gag|recitazione)\b/i;
        const detailOnlyRegex = /\b(?:texture|dettaglio|font|inchiostro|carta|trama|colore|grafica|mistero del dettaglio|piega|poster|decorative_detail|informational_surface|percorso|posizione)\b/i;
        const landingRegex = /\b(?:partecipate|scoprire|vi aspetta|l'evento|all'esibizione|all'attivitÃƒÂ |radunarsi|esserci|interagire|guarda|ascolta|scopri)\b/i;
        
        const semanticMentionsJoined = (result.semanticMentions || []).join(" ");
        const scriptText = result.script || "";
        const selectedEventText = result.selectedEvent || "";
        const humanVerdictTextRaw = result.viralAudit?.humanVerdict || "";
        
        let eventIntentScore = 0;
        let detailIntentScore = 0;
        let landingScore = 0;

        // 1. Assegna punteggi in base a selectedEvent
        if (eventCoreRegex.test(selectedEventText)) eventIntentScore += 5;
        if (detailOnlyRegex.test(selectedEventText)) detailIntentScore += 3;

        // 2. Assegna punteggi in base allo script e landing
        if (eventCoreRegex.test(scriptText)) {
          landingScore += 2;
          eventIntentScore += 1;
        }
        if (landingRegex.test(scriptText)) {
          landingScore += 3;
        }
        if (detailOnlyRegex.test(scriptText)) {
          detailIntentScore += 1;
        }

        // 3. Verifica i pareri umani (humanVerdict)
        if (/(?:focus|nucleo|centrato|elemento|protagonista).*(?:dettaglio|decorative_detail|informational_surface|percorso|solo)/i.test(humanVerdictTextRaw)) {
          detailIntentScore += 5;
          landingScore -= 3;
        }
        if (/(core_action|evento|esperienza).*(?:protagonista|centro|focus)/i.test(humanVerdictTextRaw)) {
          landingScore += 3;
        }
        
        // Log diagnostico interno su validationTrace
        if (result.validationTrace) {
           (result.validationTrace as any).intentScores = { eventIntentScore, detailIntentScore, landingScore };
        }

        const hasRealEvent = eventCoreRegex.test(textInput) || eventCoreRegex.test(semanticMentionsJoined);
        
        // 4. Regola Decisionale del Flusso basata su Intent Scoring
        let isFlowBroken = false;
        
        const isPerformanceIntent = coreIntentClassification?.coreIntent === "PERFORMANCE";
        const isEventExplicitlyRequested = (eventCategory === "EVENTO REALE" || eventCategory === "ESPERIENZA CONCRETA") && !isPerformanceIntent;

        const textToAuditHierarchy = (result.viralAudit?.humanVerdict || "") + " " + 
                                     (result.viralAudit?.strategyReasoning || "") + " " + 
                                     (result.viralAudit?.finalPromptVerdict || "");

        const scriptsToAudit = (result.script || "") + " " + (result.alternativePrompt || "") + " " + (result.selectedEvent || "") + " " + (result.viralAudit?.humanVerdict || "");
        const forbiddenDetailFocusRegex = /\b(?:percorso|dettaglio|poster|texture|inchiostro|carta|cartello|posizione|indicazioni|decorative_detail|informational_surface)\b/i;
        const validActionFocusRegex = /\b(?:incontro|festa|evento|celebrazione|raduno|radunarsi|partecipazione|esperienza|visita|laboratorio|core_action|primary_real_world_activity|performance|esibizione|recitazione|comedy|sketch|battuta|payoff|gag)\b/i;

        if (isEventExplicitlyRequested) {
          const detailFocusScore = (scriptsToAudit.match(new RegExp(forbiddenDetailFocusRegex.source, "gi")) || []).length;
          const actionFocusScore = (scriptsToAudit.match(new RegExp(validActionFocusRegex.source, "gi")) || []).length;
          
          const humanVerdictLower = String(result.viralAudit?.humanVerdict || "").toLowerCase();
          const hasForbiddenInVerdict = forbiddenDetailFocusRegex.test(humanVerdictLower);
          const hasValidInVerdict = validActionFocusRegex.test(humanVerdictLower);

          // MANDATORY PRIORITY CHECK (LOGGING ONLY - NO REGENERATION LOOP)
          if (detailFocusScore > actionFocusScore) {
            logger.warn("[EVENT_ALIGNMENT_SUBOPTIMAL]", {
              eventCategory,
              detailFocusScore,
              actionFocusScore
            });
            
            // Forzatura silenziosa se siamo in un evento: l'azione deve prevalere.
            // Se eravamo arrivati qui con punteggio squilibrato, significa che Layer 2 
            // non ha rewritto o il rewrite non ÃƒÂ¨ bastato a coprire selectedEvent/humanVerdict.
            // Invece di rigenerare (instabile), accettiamo il cleanup di Layer 3.
          }

          // Se ÃƒÂ¨ EVENTO REALE, l'azione deve ALMENO pareggiare o dominare
          if (actionFocusScore < detailFocusScore || (hasForbiddenInVerdict && !hasValidInVerdict) || landingScore < 2) {
            isFlowBroken = true;
          }
        } else if (hasRealEvent && !isPerformanceIntent && (detailIntentScore >= eventIntentScore || landingScore < 2)) {
          isFlowBroken = true;
        }

        // Degradazione del vecchio check a supporto secondario
        const badHierarchyRegex = /supporto ÃƒÂ¨ noioso|non ÃƒÂ¨ il testo|vero focus ÃƒÂ¨ il dettaglio|dettaglio ÃƒÂ¨ il vero nucleo|vero focus ÃƒÂ¨ (?:solo\s+)?(?:il|la)\s+(?:decorazione|sfondo|dettaglio)/i;
        
        const hierarchyTextViolation = badHierarchyRegex.test(textToAuditHierarchy);

        const isSelectionError = 
          result.selectionError === true || 
          result.validationTrace?.selectionError === true ||
          hierarchyTextViolation ||
          isFlowBroken ||
          (result.viralAudit?.strategyReasoning && /ERRORE DI SELEZIONE|SELECTION ERROR/i.test(result.viralAudit.strategyReasoning));

        if (isSelectionError && !structuralFailed) {
          structuralFailed = true;
          const detailFocusScoreSummary = (scriptsToAudit.match(new RegExp(forbiddenDetailFocusRegex, "gi")) || []).length;
          const actionFocusScoreSummary = (scriptsToAudit.match(new RegExp(validActionFocusRegex, "gi")) || []).length;

          structuralFailReason = (isEventExplicitlyRequested && isFlowBroken)
            ? `Action Hierarchy Violation: Event logic applied outside compatible content class. (Detail Score: ${detailFocusScoreSummary}, Action Score: ${actionFocusScoreSummary}, Landing Score: ${landingScore}). Devi centrare script sull'azione reale (primary_real_world_activity, core_action) NON su decorative_detail/informational_surface.`
            : (isFlowBroken 
              ? `EVENT FLOW BROKEN (IntentScore -> Event: ${eventIntentScore}, Detail: ${detailIntentScore}, Landing: ${landingScore}): Il contenuto ha un evento reale, ma il focus narrativo diverge sul dettaglio visivo.`
              : "SELECTION ERROR: Secondary detail prioritized over primary Event/Experience OR informational container logically separated from its details.");
          
          if (!result.validationTrace) {
            result.validationTrace = {
              structuralFailTriggered: true,
              reason: structuralFailReason,
              regenerationCount: attempts - 1,
              finalPassSource: "first_try",
              selectionError: true
            };
          } else {
            result.validationTrace.selectionError = true;
            result.validationTrace.structuralFailTriggered = true;
          }
          result.selectionError = true;
        }
      }

        // Bypass/Boost structural violation check (NEW)
        if (useBypass || viralBoost50k) {
          const aiPromptText = result.aiPrompts || "";
          // Check for creative elements that are forbidden in aiPrompts even during bypass/boost
          const creativeElementsRegex =
            /overlay|emoji|3d|testo a schermo|scritta|titolo|new scene|scena inventata|animazione artificiale/i;
          if (creativeElementsRegex.test(aiPromptText)) {
            bypassViolation = true;
            structuralFailReason =
              "BYPASS/BOOST VIOLATION: Creative elements (overlay, emoji, 3D, new scenes) detected in aiPrompts. These must only exist in alternativePrompt.";
            logger.warn(
              "[Gemini] Bypass/Boost violation detected in aiPrompts on try " +
                attempts,
            );
          }
        }

        // Hard Regex check on generative output for promo words to enforce continuity
        const badWordsRegex =
          /ecco il segreto|inauguriamo|\bscopri\s+(?:il|la)\b|ti aspettiamo|venite a|non perderti|non perdere l'occasione|honey aesthetic|honey macro aesthetic|warm sun|scenic entrance|lush marsh|lush wetlands|rustic table|scenic nature|brochure turistica/i;
          const generativeFields = [
            result.script,
            result.aiPrompts,
            result.soraPrompt12s,
            result.klingPrompt10s,
            result.klingPrompt15s,
            result.seedancePrompt15s,
            result.sendancePrompt15s,
            result.veo3Prompt8s,
            result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s,
            result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s,
            result.klingPrompt,
            result.veoPrompt,
            result.alternativePrompt,
          result.coverPrompt,
          result.promptSora15s,
          result.promptSora12s,
          result.promptKling,
          result.promptVeo,
          result.promptCover,
        ];
        const generativeText = generativeFields
          .filter(Boolean)
          .map((v) => (typeof v === "string" ? v : JSON.stringify(v)))
          .join(" ");
        const hasPromoWords = badWordsRegex.test(generativeText);
        if (
          hasPromoWords &&
          !structuralFailed &&
          !bypassViolation &&
          !staticViolation
        ) {
          structuralFailed = true;
          structuralFailReason =
            "CONTINUITY FAIL-SAFE: Found promo tourism words or aesthetic in generative fields despite being told not to";
          logger.warn(
            "[Gemini] Generative fields promo word continuity regex triggered on try " +
              attempts,
          );
        }

        let applyFailSafe = false;

        // FAIL-SAFE LOGIC (PROBLEM A pt 2)
        // Se siamo al terzo tentativo (attempts >= 2) e falliamo per motivi borderline, salviamo.
        if (attempts >= 2 && (structuralFailed || fidelityFailed || staticViolation)) {
           const isAligned = result?.sourceAnchor?.isAligned === true;

           // Critical Event Core failures are NOT borderline
           const isCriticalEventCoreFailure = 
             structuralFailed && 
             structuralFailReason && 
             (structuralFailReason.includes("EVENT_PRIORITY_VIOLATION") || 
              structuralFailReason.includes("EVENT_CORE_MISSING_EXPERIENCE") ||
              structuralFailReason.includes("EVENT_ACCESS_DOMINANT_SELECTED_EVENT") ||
              structuralFailReason.includes("ALT_PROMPT_NO_EXPERIENCE_FOLLOWUP") ||
              structuralFailReason.includes("DOMINANCE_PLAN_BROKEN") ||
              structuralFailReason.includes("CONTENT_HIERARCHY_BROKEN"));

           // Valutiamo se le violazioni sono bypassabili. 
           // Non bypassiamo selectionError o bypassViolation grave.
           const isSelectionError = 
             result?.selectionError === true || 
             result?.validationTrace?.selectionError === true ||
             (result?.viralAudit?.strategyReasoning && /ERRORE DI SELEZIONE|SELECTION ERROR/i.test(result.viralAudit.strategyReasoning));

           const isBorderlineFailure = (staticViolation || fidelityFailed || structuralFailed) && !isSelectionError && !bypassViolation && !isCriticalEventCoreFailure;
           
           const isStrictStatic = isStrictStaticSourceType(payloadSourceType);
           
           if (isAligned && isBorderlineFailure && !isStrictStatic) {
              logger.warn(`[Gemini] FAIL-SAFE ACTIVATED: Accepting borderline failure on attempt ${attempts} because sourceAnchor is aligned. (StaticViolation: ${staticViolation}, FidelityFailed: ${fidelityFailed}, StructuralFailed: ${structuralFailed})`);
              applyFailSafe = true;
           }
        }

        normalizeGeneratedPromptFields(result);
        populateCanonicalPromptFallbacks(result);
        applyTechnicalTraceFields(result, audioAnchor);
        emitCriticalExamInputAudit(result, logger);
        result.criticalExamReport = buildCriticalExamReport(result, audioAnchor, truthStatus);
        result.finalJudgeDecision = result.finalJudgeDecision || "";
        result.finalJudgeReasoning = result.finalJudgeReasoning || "";
        result.repairInstructions = Array.isArray(result.repairInstructions) ? result.repairInstructions : [];

        // --- LAYER 3: SUPREME VIRAL VALIDATOR ---
        // Se tutto sembra a posto (o se fail-safe ha salvato), chiediamo al SVV il verdetto finale.
        if (
          failedChecks.length === 0 &&
          !(
            (fidelityFailed ||
            structuralFailed ||
            bypassViolation ||
            staticViolation) &&
            !applyFailSafe
          )
        ) {
          try {
            const { runSupremeViralValidator } = await import('./analysis');
            if (onProgress) onProgress("Validazione finale SVV in corso...");
            const svvResponse = await runSupremeViralValidator(apiKey, result, sourceTypeLocked, contentHierarchy, modelTier, trace);
            if (svvResponse && svvResponse.svv) {
              result.svv = svvResponse.svv;
              result.finalJudgeDecision = result.svv.finalJudgeDecision || "";
              result.finalJudgeReasoning = result.svv.finalJudgeReasoning || result.svv.reason || "";
              result.repairInstructions = Array.isArray(result.svv.repairInstructions)
                ? result.svv.repairInstructions
                : (Array.isArray(result.svv.actions) ? result.svv.actions : []);
              if (result.svv.verdict === "REJECT") {
                structuralFailed = true;
                structuralFailReason = `SUPREME_VIRAL_VALIDATOR_REJECT: ${result.svv.reason}`;
                if (result.sourceAnchor) {
                  const priorReason = typeof result.sourceAnchor.reason === "string" ? result.sourceAnchor.reason : "";
                  result.sourceAnchor.reason = priorReason
                    ? `${priorReason} | Final SVV reject: ${result.svv.reason}`
                    : `Final SVV reject: ${result.svv.reason}`;
                }
                result.finalPromptVerdict = "REVIEW_REQUIRED_SVV_REJECT";
                logger.error(`[SVV] REJECT Decision: ${result.svv.reason}`);
                break; // Stop immediatamente il loop, output bocciato, va in fallback/degraded
              } else if (result.svv.verdict === "RETRY") {
                 structuralFailed = true;
                 structuralFailReason = `SUPREME_VIRAL_VALIDATOR_RETRY: ${result.svv.reason}`;
                 if (result.sourceAnchor) {
                   const priorReason = typeof result.sourceAnchor.reason === "string" ? result.sourceAnchor.reason : "";
                   result.sourceAnchor.reason = priorReason
                     ? `${priorReason} | Final SVV retry: ${result.svv.reason}`
                     : `Final SVV retry: ${result.svv.reason}`;
                 }
                 logger.warn(`[SVV] RETRY Decision: ${result.svv.reason}`);
                 // Proseguiamo con il loop cosÃƒÂ¬ fa il retry
              } else {
                 logger.info(`[SVV] PUBLISH Decision: ${result.svv.reason}`);
                 structuralFailed = false;
                 fidelityFailed = false;
                 staticViolation = false;
                 bypassViolation = false;
                 break; // Successo totale, possiamo uscire dal loop di retry
              }
            }
          } catch (e) {
            logger.error("Error running SVV", e);
          }
        }

        if (
          failedChecks.length > 0 ||
          ((fidelityFailed ||
            structuralFailed ||
            bypassViolation ||
            staticViolation) &&
            !applyFailSafe &&
            attempts < maxAttempts)
        ) {
          if (
            (fidelityFailed ||
              structuralFailed ||
              bypassViolation ||
              staticViolation) &&
            !applyFailSafe &&
            attempts < maxAttempts
          ) {
            logger.warn(
              `[Gemini] Fidelity/Structural check failed (attempt ${attempts}). StructuralFailed: ${structuralFailed} (${structuralFailReason}), FidelityFailed: ${fidelityFailed}, BypassViolation: ${bypassViolation}, StaticViolation: ${staticViolation}. Retrying...`,
              { debug, validationTrace: result.validationTrace },
            );
            lastFailReason = structuralFailReason || "Violazione di fedeltÃƒÂ  (Hallucination/Inference) rilevata nel promptInventory.";
            continue;
          }

          if (failedChecks.length > 0) {
            logger.error(
              `[Gemini] Validation failed for checks: ${failedChecks.join(", ")}`,
              { debug },
            );
            throw new Error(
              `VALIDATION_FAILED: The generated output failed critical quality checks: ${failedChecks.join(", ")}. Forcing regeneration.`,
            );
          }
        }
      }

      // If we are here, either it passed or we reached max attempts

      // Mandatory enforcement: if promo words or structural failures exist in the final generative output
      const finalBadWordsRegex =
        /ecco il segreto|inauguriamo|\bscopri\s+(?:il|la)\b|ti aspettiamo|venite a|non perderti|non perdere l'occasione|honey aesthetic|honey macro aesthetic|warm sun|scenic entrance|lush marsh|lush wetlands|rustic table|scenic nature|brochure turistica/i;
      const finalGenerativeFields = [
        result.script,
        result.aiPrompts,
        result.soraPrompt12s,
        result.klingPrompt10s,
        result.klingPrompt15s,
        result.seedancePrompt15s,
        result.sendancePrompt15s,
        result.veo3Prompt8s,
        result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s,
        result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s,
        result.klingPrompt,
        result.veoPrompt,
        result.alternativePrompt,
        result.coverPrompt,
        result.promptSora15s,
        result.promptSora12s,
        result.promptKling,
        result.promptVeo,
        result.promptCover,
      ];
      const finalGenerativeText = finalGenerativeFields
        .filter(Boolean)
        .map((v) => (typeof v === "string" ? v : JSON.stringify(v)))
        .join(" ");
      hasPromoWordsFinal = finalBadWordsRegex.test(finalGenerativeText);

      sessionFailed =
        structuralFailed || bypassViolation || hasPromoWordsFinal;

      if (!result.validationTrace) {
        result.validationTrace = {
          strategicStrategy: strategicManifest.strategy,
          intentPreserved: !structuralFailed,
          structuralFailTriggered: sessionFailed,
          reason:
            structuralFailReason ||
            (hasPromoWordsFinal
              ? "Hard Regex forced failure"
              : "System auto-filled"),
          regenerationCount: attempts - 1,
          finalPassSource:
            attempts === 1 ? "first_try" : "regenerated_after_fail",
        };
      } else {
        result.validationTrace.strategicStrategy = strategicManifest.strategy;
        result.validationTrace.intentPreserved = !structuralFailed;
        result.validationTrace.structuralFailTriggered = sessionFailed;
        result.validationTrace.reason =
          structuralFailReason || result.validationTrace.reason;
        result.validationTrace.regenerationCount = attempts - 1;
        result.validationTrace.finalPassSource =
          attempts === 1 ? "first_try" : "regenerated_after_fail";
      }

      logger.info("[Gemini][StaticGate] Final runtime flags", {
        attempt: attempts,
        sourceType: payloadSourceType,
        structuralFailed,
        validationTraceStructuralFailTriggered:
          result.validationTrace?.structuralFailTriggered,
        viralAuditEnforcementPass: result.viralAudit?.enforcementPass,
      });

      if (sessionFailed) {
        if (!result.viralAudit)
          result.viralAudit = {
            signature: "SYSTEM_FORCED",
            enforcementMarker: "FAIL",
            strategyReasoning: "Fallback triggered",
            enforcementPass: false,
          };
        result.viralAudit.enforcementPass = false;

        // Fallback mechanism: Sanitize aiPrompts on persistent failure
        if (attempts >= maxAttempts && (structuralFailed || bypassViolation)) {
          logger.warn(
            "[Gemini] Applying fallback sanitization to aiPrompts after maxAttempts",
          );
          const isStaticPayload = isStrictStaticSourceType(result.sourceType);
          const sanitizeFinalPrompt = (prompt: string) => {
            return isStaticPayload
              ? stripStaticSourceViolations(prompt, result.visibleSurfaceElements, result.eventQualitySelector?.eventCategory)
              : prompt;
          };

          const aiPromptsSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(result.aiPrompts);
          const soraPrompt15sSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.promptSora15s || result.promptSora12s || result.aiPrompts,
          );
          const soraPrompt12sSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.promptSora12s || result.aiPrompts,
          );
          const klingPrompt10sSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.klingPrompt10s || result["prompt_kling_10s"] || result["kling_prompt_10s"] || buildPromptFromBeat(result, "kling10"),
          );
          const klingPromptSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.klingPrompt15s || result.promptKling || result.klingPrompt || buildPromptFromBeat(result, "kling15"),
          );
          const seedancePrompt15sSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.seedancePrompt15s || result.sendancePrompt15s || result.promptSeedance15s || result.promptSendance15s || result["prompt_seedance_15s"] || result["prompt_sendance_15s"] || buildPromptFromBeat(result, "seedance15"),
          );
          const veoPromptSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.veo3Prompt8s || result.promptVeo || result.veoPrompt || result.aiPrompts,
          );
          const veo3Prompt8sSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.veo3Prompt8s || result.promptVeo || result.veoPrompt || buildPromptFromBeat(result, "veo8"),
          );
          const veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8sSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s || result.promptVeo3ExtensionPart1_8s || result["prompt_veo3_extension_part1_8s"] || result["veo3_extension_part1_8s"] || buildPromptFromBeat(result, "veoExt1"),
          );
          const veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8sSanitized = sanitizeFinalPrompt(
            result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s || result.promptVeo3ExtensionPart2_8s || result["prompt_veo3_extension_part2_8s"] || result["veo3_extension_part2_8s"] || buildPromptFromBeat(result, "veoExt2"),
          );

          result.aiPrompts = aiPromptsSanitized;
          result.promptSora15s = soraPrompt15sSanitized;
          result.promptSora12s = soraPrompt12sSanitized;
          result.promptKling = klingPromptSanitized;
          result.promptVeo = veoPromptSanitized;
          result.soraPrompt15s = soraPrompt15sSanitized;
          result.soraPrompt12s = soraPrompt12sSanitized;
          result.klingPrompt10s = klingPrompt10sSanitized;
          result.klingPrompt15s = klingPromptSanitized;
          result.seedancePrompt15s = seedancePrompt15sSanitized;
          result.sendancePrompt15s = seedancePrompt15sSanitized;
          result.veo3Prompt8s = veo3Prompt8sSanitized;
          result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s = veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8sSanitized;
          result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s = veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8sSanitized;
          result.klingPrompt = klingPromptSanitized;
          result.veoPrompt = veoPromptSanitized;
        }
      }

      result.text = response.text; // Keep reference to raw text
      break;
    }

    if (onProgress)
      onProgress(`Sanitizzazione e controllo sicurezza dei prompt in corso...`);

    // Mapping of key suffix to top-level property name in FULL/LIGHT schemas
      const promptMapping: Record<string, string> = {
      sora15s: "promptSora15s",
      sora12s: "promptSora12s",
      kling: "promptKling",
      veo: "promptVeo",
      cover: "coverPrompt",
    };

    // Process sequentially instead of Promise.all to respect the 15 RPM API limit
    for (const [suffix, topKey] of Object.entries(promptMapping)) {
      // Check for top-level keys first (FULL/LIGHT schemas)
      if (result[topKey]) {
        logger.info(`[Gemini] Sanitizing top-level prompt: ${topKey}`);
        let cleaned = result[topKey];
        cleaned = await rewriteDangerousPrompt(cleaned, apiKey);
        cleaned = purifyPromptAntiEmoji(cleaned);
        result[topKey] = cleaned;
      }

      // Also check for legacy nested prompts if any
      if (result.prompts && result.prompts[suffix]) {
        logger.info(`[Gemini] Sanitizing nested prompt for key: ${suffix}`);
        let cleaned = result.prompts[suffix];
        cleaned = await rewriteDangerousPrompt(cleaned, apiKey);
        cleaned = purifyPromptAntiEmoji(cleaned);
        result.prompts[suffix] = cleaned;
      }
    }

    // --- PHASE 2.5: OUTPUT COHERENCE & ON-THE-FLY CORRECTIONS ---
    
    // 1. Honesty check: if no audio is analyzed, force transcriptSource to non-audio
    if (!result.transcriptSource || result.transcriptSource === "VERIFIED_AUDIO") {
        if (result.dialogueConfidence < 40) {
            result.transcriptSource = "VISUAL_INFERENCE";
        }
    }

    const lacksLockedAudio = !audioAnchor || audioAnchor.dialogueLockStatus !== "AUDIO_LOCKED";

    if (lacksLockedAudio) {
        result.transcriptSource = "VISUAL_INFERENCE";
        result.scriptSourceMode = "FRAME_VISUAL_DESCRIPTION";
        result.dialogueConfidence = Math.min(result.dialogueConfidence || 0, 39);
        if (result.originalScript) {
            result.originalScript = sanitizeNonLockedDialogueScript(result.originalScript);
        }
        if (result.script && (/[\\"'“”«»]/u.test(result.script) || /\p{Lu}[\p{L}'-]{1,30}\s*:/u.test(result.script))) {
            result.script = sanitizeNonLockedDialogueScript(result.script);
        }
    }

    // 2. Script Optimization Status Reflection
    if (result.scriptOptimizationStatus === "ORIGINAL_SCRIPT_PREFERRED") {
        result.script = result.originalScript;
    }

    const hasRichVerifiedAudioScript =
      !!audioAnchor?.audioVerified &&
      extractNarrativeBeats(result.originalScript || "").length >= 4;

    if (hasRichVerifiedAudioScript) {
        const currentOptimizedBeats = extractNarrativeBeats(result.script || "");
        if (currentOptimizedBeats.length <= 2) {
            result.script = buildFaithfulBeatScript(result.originalScript || "");
            result.scriptCompressionMode = "DESCRIPTIVE_SAFE";
        }
    }

    const beatAlignedScript =
      hasRichVerifiedAudioScript && String(result.script || "").trim().length > 0
        ? buildFaithfulBeatScript(result.originalScript || "")
        : "";

    if (beatAlignedScript) {
        result.aiPrompts = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.aiPrompts || "", beatAlignedScript);
        if (typeof result.promptSora12s === "string") {
            result.promptSora12s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.promptSora12s, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.soraPrompt12s === "string") {
            result.soraPrompt12s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.soraPrompt12s, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.klingPrompt10s === "string") {
            result.klingPrompt10s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.klingPrompt10s, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.klingPrompt15s === "string") {
            result.klingPrompt15s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.klingPrompt15s, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.promptKling === "string") {
            result.promptKling = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.promptKling, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.klingPrompt === "string") {
            result.klingPrompt = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.klingPrompt, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.seedancePrompt15s === "string") {
            result.seedancePrompt15s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.seedancePrompt15s, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.sendancePrompt15s === "string") {
            result.sendancePrompt15s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.sendancePrompt15s, beatAlignedScript);
        }
        if (typeof result.veo3Prompt8s === "string") {
            result.veo3Prompt8s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.veo3Prompt8s, beatAlignedScript, true);
        }
        if (typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s === "string") {
            result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s, beatAlignedScript, true);
        }
        if (typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s === "string") {
            result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s, beatAlignedScript, true);
        }
        if (typeof result.promptVeo === "string") {
            result.promptVeo = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.promptVeo, beatAlignedScript, true);
        }
        if (typeof result.veoPrompt === "string") {
            result.veoPrompt = ensureBeatArcPrompt(result.veoPrompt, beatAlignedScript, true);
        }
    } else {
        result.aiPrompts = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.aiPrompts || "");
        if (typeof result.promptSora12s === "string") result.promptSora12s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.promptSora12s);
        if (typeof result.soraPrompt12s === "string") result.soraPrompt12s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.soraPrompt12s);
        if (typeof result.klingPrompt10s === "string") result.klingPrompt10s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.klingPrompt10s);
        if (typeof result.klingPrompt15s === "string") result.klingPrompt15s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.klingPrompt15s);
        if (typeof result.promptKling === "string") result.promptKling = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.promptKling);
        if (typeof result.klingPrompt === "string") result.klingPrompt = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.klingPrompt);
        if (typeof result.seedancePrompt15s === "string") result.seedancePrompt15s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.seedancePrompt15s);
        if (typeof result.sendancePrompt15s === "string") result.sendancePrompt15s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.sendancePrompt15s);
        if (typeof result.veo3Prompt8s === "string") result.veo3Prompt8s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.veo3Prompt8s);
        if (typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s === "string") result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.veo3ExtensionPart1Prompt8s);
        if (typeof result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s === "string") result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.veo3ExtensionPart2Prompt8s);
        if (typeof result.promptVeo === "string") result.promptVeo = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.promptVeo);
        if (typeof result.veoPrompt === "string") result.veoPrompt = softenLipSyncLanguage(result.veoPrompt);
    }

    normalizeGeneratedPromptFields(result);
    populateCanonicalPromptFallbacks(result);

    result.finalScriptNormalized =
      typeof result.script === "string" && result.script.trim().length > 0
        ? result.script
        : (result.originalScript || "");

    // 3. Alternative Prompt Logic (Strict)
    const viralScoreNum = parseFloat(result.viralScore?.toString() || "0");
    const isGoodVideo = viralScoreNum >= 7.5;
    const isGeneraDecision = result.operationalDecision === "GENERA";
    const isFaithfulEnough = (result.scriptFaithfulnessScore || 0) >= 85;

    const skipAlternative = isGoodVideo && isGeneraDecision && isFaithfulEnough;

    if (skipAlternative) {
        result.alternativePrompt = "";
        result.finalPromptVerdict = "PASS_NO_ALTERNATIVE_NEEDED";
        if (result.operationalDecision === "GENERA" && result.sourceAnchor?.isAligned === true) {
            result.altHook = "";
            result.altScene = "";
            result.altTwist = "";
            result.readyAlternative = [];
            if (!result.parsedKit) result.parsedKit = {};
            result.parsedKit.altHook = "";
            result.parsedKit.altScene = "";
            result.parsedKit.altTwist = "";
            result.parsedKit.readyAlternative = [];
        }
    } else {
        if (!result.alternativePrompt || result.alternativePrompt.trim() === "") {
             logger.warn("[Gemini] Fallback: creating minimal alternative prompt.");
             result.alternativePrompt = `POV transformation. Focus on the emotional shift or the unexpected detail in the scene.`;
        }
    }

    const isInformational = 
      result.operationalDecision === "RIVEDI" ||
      result.operationalDecision === "BLCCA" ||
      result.operationalDecision === "GENERA_CON_AVVERTENZA";
    
    const isEnforcementPassFalse = result.viralAudit?.enforcementPass === false;
    const isStructuralFailTriggered = result.validationTrace?.structuralFailTriggered === true;
    
    const requiresAlternativePrompt = !skipAlternative && (isInformational || isEnforcementPassFalse || isStructuralFailTriggered);

    if (requiresAlternativePrompt) {
        if (result.sourceAnchor) {
            result.sourceAnchor.alternativeGenerated = true;
        }
    }

    // Problem 4 - Patch minima optimizedScript
    const isStaticPayload = result.sourceType === "STATIC_IMAGE" || result.sourceType === "POSTER" || result.sourceType === "FLYER";
    
    if (isStaticPayload) {
        if (!result.script || result.script.length < 10) {
             const anchor = result.visibleSurfaceElements?.[0] || result.semanticMentions?.[0] || "l'elemento centrale";
             const fallbackScript = `[00:00-00:02] Hook: L'immagine mostra chiaramente ${anchor}.\n[00:02-00:04] Sviluppo: Osserviamo un singolo dettaglio visivo coerente.\n[00:04-00:05] Chiusura: Il quadro si chiude in modo funzionale sul messaggio.`;
             result.script = fallbackScript;
             if (!result.originalScript) result.originalScript = fallbackScript;
        }
    }

    if (structuralFailed || sessionFailed) {
      truthStatus.mode = "DEGRADED_MODE";
      truthStatus.severity = (truthStatus.severity === "CRITICAL") ? "CRITICAL" : "MEDIUM";
      truthStatus.fallbackActive = true;
      truthStatus.userMessage = `Il contenuto ÃƒÂ¨ stato generato con alcune restrizioni di fedeltÃƒÂ  (Status: DEGRADED). Errore rilevato: ${structuralFailReason || (hasPromoWordsFinal ? "Regex Promo Word" : "Fidelity Fallback")}`;
    } else if (truthStatus.mode === "FULL_MODE") {
      truthStatus.userMessage = "Generazione completata con successo. Tutti i lock di sicurezza e fedeltÃƒÂ  sono stati superati.";
    }

    if (engineReliability === "DEGRADED" || engineReliability === "FAILED") {
      if (result.engineConfidence === "HIGH") result.engineConfidence = "MEDIUM";
      if (typeof result.viralScore === 'string' || typeof result.viralScore === 'number') {
        const score = parseFloat(result.viralScore.toString());
        if (score > 6.0) result.viralScore = (score * 0.8).toFixed(1);
      }
      
      const diagnosticNote = "Analisi completata con fallback: alcuni moduli di interpretazione non hanno risposto correttamente.";
      if (truthStatus && typeof truthStatus.userMessage === 'string' && !truthStatus.userMessage.includes(diagnosticNote)) {
        truthStatus.userMessage = `${diagnosticNote}\n${truthStatus.userMessage}`;
      }
      
      result.engineHonestyStatement = result.engineHonestyStatement || "";
      if (typeof result.engineHonestyStatement === 'string' && !result.engineHonestyStatement.includes(diagnosticNote)) {
        result.engineHonestyStatement = `${diagnosticNote}\n${result.engineHonestyStatement}`;
      }
    }

    applyTechnicalTraceFields(result, audioAnchor);
    if (!result.audioVerified) {
      truthStatus.mode = "DEGRADED_MODE";
      truthStatus.severity =
        truthStatus.severity === "CRITICAL"
          ? "CRITICAL"
          : compareSeverity(truthStatus.severity, "MEDIUM");
      truthStatus.fallbackActive = true;
      if (!truthStatus.failedModules.includes("AudioAnchor")) {
        truthStatus.failedModules.push("AudioAnchor");
      }
      truthStatus.reliabilityImpact = "Audio non verificato: script e prompt dialogici sono stati degradati a inferenza visiva o performance-first.";
      truthStatus.userMessage = "Analisi completata in modalita degradata: Audio Anchor non verificato, output dialogici ridotti per evitare linee inventate.";
    }
    finalizePromptFields(result);
    emitCriticalExamInputAudit(result, logger);
    result.criticalExamReport = buildCriticalExamReport(result, audioAnchor, truthStatus);
    reconcileFinalJudgeDecision(result);

    logger.info(`[FINAL_RELIABILITY_STATE]
engineReliability=${engineReliability}
warningsCount=${engineWarnings.length}
failedModules=${JSON.stringify(engineWarnings.map(w => w.module))}
fallbackUsed=${engineWarnings.some(w => w.fallbackApplied)}`);

    if (runAbortReason === 'QUOTA_EXHAUSTED') {
       throw new Error("QUOTA_EXHAUSTED: Quota Gemini esaurita: analisi interrotta senza ulteriori chiamate per evitare consumo inutile.");
    }

    return {
      ...result,
      contentHierarchy,
      text: response.text,
      modelUsed: model,
      runtimeTruthStatus: truthStatus,
      engineWarnings,
      engineReliability
    };
  };

  // I retry locali duplicati sono stati rimossi: delegato a executeWithNetworkRetry (core.ts)
  return await executeGeneration(modelTier);
}

export async function extractVideoSummary(
  file: File | undefined,
  apiKey: string,
  onProgress?: (text: string) => void,
  frames?: string[],
  modelTier: string = "flash",
  trace?: ModelUsageTrace,
  providedFileUri?: string,
  audioAnchor?: AudioAnchorResult | null,
): Promise<{
  summary: string;
  fileUri?: string;
  detectedGenre?: string;
  genreConfidence?: string;
  characterArtist?: string;
  searchQueries?: string[];
}> {
  const { ai } = getAI(apiKey);
    const plannedModel = selectModel(
      modelTier === "pro" ? "pro" : "flash",
      "flash",
      apiKey,
    );

  let parts: any[] = [];
  let fileUri: string | undefined = providedFileUri;

  if (audioAnchor?.audioVerified && audioAnchor.scriptConfidence >= 80) {
      logger.info("[AUDIO_ANCHOR_REAL_PIPELINE_INJECTED]");
      parts.push({ text: `[AUDIO_ANCHOR_VERIFIED_CONTEXT] ${audioAnchor.verifiedInlineVideoSummary}` });
  } else {
      logger.info("[AUDIO_ANCHOR_REAL_PIPELINE_CONTINUE_FRAME_ONLY]");
  }

  if (frames && frames.length > 0) {
    if (onProgress) onProgress("Analisi preliminare fotogrammi...");
    // Per ricerca di mercato non servono 60 frame, ne bastano 15 per evitare timeout in PRO
    const maxSummaryFrames = 15;
    const sampledFrames = frames.length <= maxSummaryFrames ? frames : 
      Array.from({ length: maxSummaryFrames }, (_, i) => frames[Math.floor(i * (frames.length - 1) / (maxSummaryFrames - 1))]);

    const frameParts = sampledFrames
      .map((f) => {
        const p = parseDataUrl(f);
        return p
          ? { inlineData: { mimeType: p.mimeType, data: p.data } }
          : null;
      })
      .filter(Boolean);
    parts.push(...frameParts);
  } else if (file) {
    const isVideo = file.type.startsWith("video/");
    // Deterministic upload check: If fileUri is not provided and file is large (>7MB), upload.
    if (fileUri) {
      parts.push({ fileData: { fileUri: fileUri, mimeType: file.type } });
    } else if ((isVideo && file.size > 7 * 1024 * 1024) || file.size > 20 * 1024 * 1024) {
      if (onProgress) onProgress(isVideo ? "Analisi preliminare video (upload)..." : "Analisi preliminare immagine (upload)...");
      fileUri = await uploadToGemini(file, apiKey, onProgress);
      if (fileUri) {
        await waitForFileActive(fileUri, apiKey, onProgress);
        parts.push({ fileData: { fileUri, mimeType: file.type } });
      }
    } else {
      if (onProgress) onProgress(isVideo ? "Analisi preliminare video (inlineData)..." : "Analisi preliminare immagine (inlineData)...");
      const base64 = await new Promise<string>((resolve, reject) => {
        const reader = new FileReader();
        reader.onloadend = () => resolve(reader.result as string);
        reader.onerror = () =>
          reject(new Error("Errore durante la lettura del file locale."));
        reader.readAsDataURL(file);
      });
      const p = parseDataUrl(base64);
      if (p) parts.push({ inlineData: { mimeType: p.mimeType, data: p.data } });
    }
  } else {
    return { summary: "" };
  }

  parts.push({
    text: `
    Analizza questo video e identifica i segnali esterni per la ricerca di mercato.
    
    ${ENTITY_PRIORITY_RULES}
    ${CONTEXT_VALIDATION_RULES}
    
    ISTRUZIONI:
    1. Identifica chiaramente il soggetto (es. 'carabiniere', 'ABBA', 'Boney M.').
    2. Determina il genere musicale e l'epoca basandoti sulla ENTITY PRIORITY RULE.
    3. Se riconosci l'artista/brano, il genere DEVE essere coerente (es. Boney M. -> Disco).
    4. Genera query di ricerca specifiche per YouTube per trovare video comparabili.
    5. Restituisci il risultato seguendo lo schema JSON richiesto.
  `,
  });

  const isUsingFileUri = !!fileUri;
  const timeoutMs = 120000; // was: isUsingFileUri ? 120000 : 45000;

  const response = await executeWithNetworkRetry(
    (currentAi, dynamicModel) =>
      currentAi.models.generateContent({
        model: dynamicModel || plannedModel,
        contents: { parts },
        config: {
          responseMimeType: "application/json",
          responseSchema: EXTERNAL_SIGNAL_EXTRACTION_SCHEMA,
        },
      }),
    0, // Will be ignored by maxRetriesPerModel, but we pass 0 just in case
    undefined,
    timeoutMs, 
    apiKey,
    onProgress,
    plannedModel,
    trace,
    "Video Summary Extraction",
    modelTier,
    false,
    "AUXILIARY" // Reduce importance to have less retries
  );

  const parsed = safeParseJSON(response.text || "{}");
  const summary = `${parsed.characterArtist || ""} - ${parsed.theme || ""} (${parsed.contentType || ""}). Genre: ${parsed.detectedGenre || "Unknown"}`;

  return {
    summary,
    fileUri,
    detectedGenre: parsed.detectedGenre,
    genreConfidence: parsed.genreConfidence,
    characterArtist: parsed.characterArtist,
    searchQueries: parsed.searchQueries,
  };
}

export async function generateCover(
  prompt: string,
  aspectRatio: string = "16:9",
  referenceImage?: string,
  hookText?: string,
  pomelli?: any,
  apiKey?: string,
  modelTier: string = "flash",
  trace?: ModelUsageTrace,
): Promise<string> {
  const executeGeneration = async () => {
    const { ai } = getAI(apiKey);
    const model = "gemini-flash-latest";

    // The prompt might have been edited by the user, so we sanitize and rewrite it again
    let optimizedPrompt = await rewriteDangerousPrompt(prompt, apiKey);
    optimizedPrompt = purifyPromptAntiEmoji(optimizedPrompt);

    const fullPrompt = hookText
      ? `${optimizedPrompt}. Include the following text overlay: "${hookText}"`
      : optimizedPrompt;

    const parts: any[] = [{ text: fullPrompt }];

    if (referenceImage) {
      const p = parseDataUrl(referenceImage);
      if (p) parts.push({ inlineData: { mimeType: p.mimeType, data: p.data } });
    }

    const response = await executeWithNetworkRetry(async (currentAi, dynamicModel) =>
        currentAi.models.generateContent({
        model: dynamicModel || model,
          contents: { parts },
          config: {
            imageConfig: {
              aspectRatio: aspectRatio as any,
            },
          },
        }),
      3,
      undefined,
      300000,
      apiKey,
      undefined,
      model,
      trace,
      "Cover Generation",
      "flash",
    );

    console.log(
      "[Gemini] generateCover response:",
      JSON.stringify(response, null, 2),
    );

    if (response.candidates && response.candidates[0]) {
      const candidate = response.candidates[0];
      if (candidate.finishReason === "SAFETY") {
        throw new Error(
          "Generazione bloccata dai filtri di sicurezza di Google. Prova a modificare il prompt rimuovendo nomi di persone famose o brand.",
        );
      }
      if (
        candidate.finishReason === "IMAGE_OTHER" ||
        candidate.finishReason === "OTHER"
      ) {
        throw new Error(
          "La generazione ÃƒÂ¨ stata rifiutata dal modello (IMAGE_OTHER). Questo accade spesso se il prompt evoca troppo direttamente una celebritÃƒÂ  o un brand protetto. Prova a usare descrizioni piÃƒÂ¹ generiche.",
        );
      }
      if (candidate.content && candidate.content.parts) {
        let textResponse = "";
        for (const part of candidate.content.parts) {
          if (part.inlineData) {
            return `data:${part.inlineData.mimeType || "image/png"};base64,${part.inlineData.data}`;
          }
          if (part.text) {
            textResponse += part.text + " ";
          }
        }
        if (textResponse) {
          console.warn(
            "[Gemini] generateCover returned text instead of image:",
            textResponse,
          );
          throw new Error(
            `Il modello ha restituito testo invece di un'immagine: ${textResponse.substring(0, 100)}...`,
          );
        }
      }
    }

    throw new Error("Nessuna immagine generata dal modello.");
  };

  return await executeGeneration();
}

export async function refinePromptWithGoal(
  prompt: string,
  goal: string,
  apiKey?: string,
  modelTier: string = "flash",
): Promise<string> {
  const executeRefinement = async (currentModelTier: string) => {
    const { ai } = getAI(apiKey);
    const model = selectModel(
      currentModelTier === "pro" ? "pro" : "flash",
      "flash",
      apiKey,
    );

    const fullPrompt = `
      Raffina questo prompt video per raggiungere questo obiettivo: "\${goal}".
      Prompt originale: "\${prompt}"
      
      Mantieni lo stile tecnico e cinematografico. Restituisci SOLO il prompt raffinato.
    `;

    const response = await executeWithNetworkRetry(
      () =>
        ai.models.generateContent({
          model,
          contents: { parts: [{ text: fullPrompt }] },
        }),
      3,
      undefined,
      300000,
    );

    let refined = sanitizePrompt(response.text || "", apiKey, model);
    refined = await rewriteDangerousPrompt(refined, apiKey);
    return purifyPromptAntiEmoji(refined);
  };

  try {
    return await executeRefinement(modelTier);
  } catch (err: any) {
    throw err;
  }
}

